@startuml Enhanced Sandbox Environment Setup Sequence

!theme plain
title SABER Enhanced Docker Sandbox Environment Setup - Multi-Container Support

actor Agent
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "TaskManager" as TM
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM_EP
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM
participant "SandboxManager" as SBMGR
participant "DockerSandboxEnvironment" as DSE
participant "Docker Compose" as DC
participant "Target Services" as TS

== Episode Initialization with Multi-Container Environment ==

Agent -> SM: POST /session/{id}/start-episode\n{task_id: "dvwa_sql_injection"}
activate SM

SM -> TM: get_task(task_id)
activate TM

note over TM
TaskManager loads task configuration
including environment specification
with target services
end note

TM -> SM: task_object
deactivate TM

SM -> EM: configure_for_task(session_id, task_object)
activate EM

note over EM
ExecutionManager extracts environment_spec
from task object and configures sandbox
Environment spec includes:
- execution container config
- target services (DVWA + MySQL)
- network configuration
- resource limits
end note

EM -> SBMGR: create_session_environment(session_id, environment_spec)
activate SBMGR

SBMGR -> DSE: new DockerSandboxEnvironment(session_id, environment_spec)
activate DSE

SM -> EM_EP: start_episode(session_id, task_id, initial_context)
activate EM_EP

EM_EP -> SM: episode_object
deactivate EM_EP

note over DSE
DockerSandboxEnvironment detects
multi-container configuration and
prepares Docker Compose setup
end note

DSE -> DSE: analyze_environment_spec()
DSE -> DSE: is_multi_container() -> True

== Multi-Container Environment Setup ==

DSE -> DSE: generate_compose_config()

note over DSE
Generates docker-compose.yml with:
- dvwa_webapp service (vulnerable web app)
- dvwa_database service (MySQL)
- pentesting_sandbox service (execution env)
- Internal network with no external access
- Health checks and dependencies
end note

DSE -> DC: docker-compose up -d
activate DC

DC -> TS: Start MySQL database
activate TS

note over TS
MySQL container starts with:
- DVWA database setup
- Vulnerable configuration
- Health checks enabled
end note

DC -> TS: Start DVWA web application
note over TS
DVWA container starts with:
- Depends on database
- Exposed on port 80 (internal network)
- Health checks verify web server
end note

DC -> DSE: Start execution container
note over DSE
Pentesting sandbox starts with:
- Network access to target services
- Pentesting tools available
- No external network access
- Ready for agent commands
end note

DC -> DC: Wait for all health checks
DC --> DSE: All services healthy
deactivate DC

DSE -> DSE: verify_environment_health()
DSE -> DSE: get_primary_container() -> execution container

DSE --> SBMGR: DockerSandboxEnvironment ready
deactivate DSE

SBMGR --> EM: Environment created successfully
deactivate SBMGR

EM --> TM: Execution environment ready
deactivate EM

TM -> TM: create_episode(task_id, session_id, environment)
TM --> SM: Episode created with multi-container environment
deactivate TM

SM --> Agent: 200 OK\n{episode_id, environment_info}
deactivate SM

== Agent Command Execution in Enhanced Environment ==

Agent -> SM: MCP tool call: execute_command("nmap dvwa_webapp")
activate SM

SM -> EM: execute_command(session_id, "nmap dvwa_webapp")
activate EM

EM -> SBMGR: get_session_environment(session_id)
activate SBMGR

SBMGR --> EM: DockerSandboxEnvironment
deactivate SBMGR

EM -> DSE: execute_command(["nmap", "dvwa_webapp"])
activate DSE

note over DSE
Command executes in primary container
(pentesting sandbox) with network access
to target services via Docker Compose
internal network
end note

DSE -> DSE: run_in_primary_container()
DSE --> EM: CommandResult(success=True, data="Host dvwa_webapp is up...")
deactivate DSE

EM --> SM: CommandResult
deactivate EM

SM --> Agent: MCP result with nmap output
deactivate SM

== Environment Cleanup ==

Agent -> SM: DELETE /session/{id}
activate SM

SM -> SBMGR: cleanup_session(session_id)
activate SBMGR

SBMGR -> DSE: stop()
activate DSE

DSE -> DC: docker-compose down --volumes
activate DC

DC -> TS: Stop and remove all containers
deactivate TS

DC -> DC: Remove networks and volumes
DC --> DSE: Environment cleaned up
deactivate DC

DSE --> SBMGR: Cleanup complete
deactivate DSE

SBMGR --> SM: Session cleaned up
deactivate SBMGR

SM --> Agent: 200 OK - Session terminated
deactivate SM

note over Agent, DC
Complete multi-container environment
including target services and execution
environment properly orchestrated and
cleaned up via Docker Compose
end note

@enduml
